Z||000000||WisconsinGT||09-29-2000||04:39 PM||||I was wondering if one of the reasons my car is missing would be due to the fact that my Fuel pump is bad. I notice that my car sounds like it is missing and running on fewer then six cylinders. But under load all is well. Could the fuel pump cause this? I have replaced the regulator and blueprinted the injectors. (Marren motorsports) Also, about 10 months ago I changed the fuel filter. Oh, also, I noticed that at around 2100RMP's I hear a noise that seems to go away (Sometimes) after my auto shifts. It sounds similer to fluid having a hard time getting through something. Hard to describe. Anyone have any clues? Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||09-29-2000||04:46 PM||||Smells electrical to me . Mine was missing and idling erratic, but, seemed to run on all four. It was a headlight short( the isolation relay ) causing the problem. It also made static pops on the radio when it would stumble.||||reg||1
